# Unity
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]serSettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/

# Generated by the Unity editor, not source
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
sysinfo.txt

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.app
*.unitypackage
*.exe

# Editors
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DS_Store

# Verification harness output
verification-result.txt

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Per-machine relay override read by RelayClient. Pointing your own checkout at a
# local relay must not repoint everyone else's.
relay-url.txt

# Per-machine environment for the relay child, written by deploy/local-https.ps1.
relay-env.txt

# Per-machine network mode choice (LAN/Hotspot), written by StartScreen. Each host's
# own preference, not something one checkout should impose on everyone else's.
network-mode.txt

# Per-host match settings (Random rocks / Tuning set / Rounds per match), written by the
# F4 host panel. Same reasoning as network-mode.txt.
match-settings.json

# Per-machine hotspot SSID/passphrase, written by HotspotCredentialsStore so a returning
# phone can remember this network. Each host's own credentials, not something one checkout
# should impose on everyone else's.
hotspot-credentials.json

# Per-machine room code, written by RoomCodeStore so a returning phone can rejoin the same
# room after a restart. Same reasoning as hotspot-credentials.json.
room-code.txt

# Spike output. Records one machine's run, so it is evidence rather than source.
deploy/spike/*.log

# Load-bearing, not a backstop. The certificate key for play.skiprocking.ca is published
# deliberately (docs/plans/magic-domain-replacement.md), so the risk this guards against is
# not disclosure — it is permanence. A key committed here lives in git history forever,
# removable only by a history rewrite, and GitHub's push protection is liable to reject the
# push outright. deploy/fetch-seed-cert.ps1 therefore stages the seed under
# deploy/seed-cert/ at packaging time, where these two rules keep it untracked, and
# installer.iss bakes it into the build from there — so the key reaches a player's machine
# without ever becoming a tracked object.
*.pem
*.key
deploy/seed-cert/
